sequenceDiagram
    participant CS as Charging Station (Test System)
    participant CSMS as CSMS (System under Test)

    Note over CS,CSMS: Prerequisite: The CSMS supports security profile 2 and/or 3

    CS->>CSMS: Terminate connection, then initiate TLS handshake with TLS version lower than 1.2 - Client Hello
    CSMS->>CS: Terminate connection (TLS version lower than 1.2 noticed)

    CS->>CSMS: Initiate TLS handshake with TLS version 1.2 or higher - Client Hello
    CSMS-->>CS: Server Hello (with Configured server certificate)

    opt CSMS uses security profile 3
        CS->>CSMS: Send client certificate
    end
    CS->>CSMS: Client Key Exchange, Certificate verify, Change Cipher Spec, Finished
    CSMS-->>CS: Change Cipher Spec, Finished

    CS->>CSMS: HTTP upgrade request
    Note right of CS: The HTTP request only contains a username/password combination<br>when the CSMS uses security profile 2
    CSMS-->>CS: Upgrade the connection to a (secured) WebSocket connection

    CS->>CSMS: BootNotificationRequest (reason = PowerUp, chargingStation.model = Configured model, chargingStation.vendorName = Configured vendorName)
    CSMS-->>CS: BootNotificationResponse
    Note over CSMS: Validation: BootNotificationResponse status must be Accepted

    loop For all connectors
        CS->>CSMS: StatusNotificationRequest (connectorStatus = Available)
        CSMS-->>CS: StatusNotificationResponse
        CS->>CSMS: NotifyEventRequest (trigger = Delta, actualValue = "Available", component.name = "Connector", variable.name = "AvailabilityState")
        CSMS-->>CS: NotifyEventResponse
    end
